{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_01NbM1web3Tr7uwLGZim7Lg4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Here's what was written for **Q23: Sandbox tool execution safely?**\n\n---\n\n**Key structure of the answer:**\n\n**Concept:** Sandboxing is a risk-tier framework, not a single technique. The appropriate isolation level depends on the blast radius of a bad tool call.\n\n**Three-tier model:**\n| Tier | Tool type | Approach |\n|------|-----------|----------|\n| Low | Read-only (web search, DB SELECT) | JSON schema validation + timeout only |\n| Medium | Stateful writes (INSERT, email) | Docker `--network=none`, readonly FS, idempotency via `tool_call_id` hash |\n| High | Code execution, shell, payments | E2B/Modal ephemeral microVM + input sanitization + output capping + append-only audit log + HITL gate |\n\n**Concrete tooling:** E2B (`~200ms cold-start, ~$0.19/day for 10K executions`) vs Docker (`--network=none --read-only --tmpfs /tmp`), with warm container pools as the scale optimization.\n\n**Key pitfalls called out:**\n1. Using `subprocess.run()` without network/filesystem isolation\n2. Treating sandboxing as the *only* layer (forgetting input sanitization as defense-in-depth)\n3. Missing idempotency on retries — double-committing write side-effects after timeouts\n\nNext up in the plan: **Q24: Tool failures, retries, idempotency?**"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":343,"cache_read_input_tokens":67833,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":343,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"938e1e34-b601-4f9d-97d0-2e78b0bde34f","uuid":"4a4ff7a1-c93e-4ca3-b060-3c311db581d2"}
